A||||5||Adrift||How to use a Rivet Gun?||||5||
Z||000000||Adrift||10-21-2001||11:32 AM||||I found a tool for applying rivets in my basement but can't for the life of me figure out how it works! Anyone have a webpage they can point me to or describe to me (with pictures I'm hoping) here what to do with it? I would like to rivet many things on my car down (I've been screwing everything into place now which is very annoying)<BR>Thanks<BR>Adrift<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-21-2001||11:46 AM||||Point and shoot?<BR>Go and buy some rivets of the size you want to use. When you see them, you will note that they sort of look like a nail. The pointy end of the nail will go into the head of the rivet gun in the small hole. The handle should be spring loaded is its a small rivet tool to allow the rivet to seat. In the piece to be riveted you will need to have the pieces together with a pilot hole the size of the rivet shank drilled. Insert rivet into hole and squeeze handle till the nail snaps. All done!||||reg||1
